<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zimbabwean plateau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zimbabwe plateau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zimbabwean plateau is a high plateau in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> rivers, rich in gold and suited to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herding. It was the setting of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a> and later of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> states. Accounts of the Rozvi Empire describe how its rulers controlled access to the gold-producing regions of the plateau, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> invasions in the nineteenth century destroyed the state.</p></div>
